      "reviewer_notes": "All 3 gates pass. Gate 1: liquidation_inner has 3 non-test callers (market.move L530, L597, L663); not dead code. Gate 2: BUG_BOUNTY_SCOPE.json has no trust_assumptions field; gate cannot trigger. Gate 3: market.move and ctoken_table.move are explicitly in-scope; liquidation logic is a listed focus area. Code-verified: liquidate_calculate_seize_ctokens returns seize_ctokens.floor() (L1073) which evaluates to 0 when repay amount is small relative to collateral/debt price ratio; no seized_ctokens > 0 guard exists before withdraw_ctokens call at L776; withdraw_ctokens calls split_ctoken(amount) which asserts amount > 0 at ctoken_table.move:82, reverting the entire transaction atomically. Severity maintained at Medium: the bug requires an unfavorable price-ratio condition to produce seized_ctokens = 0, and no explicit severity thresholds or client_diversity cap are defined in BUG_BOUNTY_SCOPE.json. An attacker can trigger this via the normal borrow/deposit entry points by crafting an obligation with dust debt (e.g., 1 unit of a low-price token) and high-value collateral (e.g., BTC), causing every ADL transaction targeting that obligation to revert, permanently blocking bad-debt clearance for the affected obligation.",
